# Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Product Name: F1 FlashPoint

### Overview

F1 FlashPoint is a Formula 1 insights-driven content engine that produces scroll-stopping Instagram post and video scripts designed to captivate new F1 fans. It merges high-fidelity analytics powered by FastF1 data and world-class AI-driven commentary with a copywriting engine that emulates viral creators (e.g., @wtf1official). It also automates visual content creation and posting via Instagram's API. The entire system will be deployed on Render with strict budget and security constraints.

---

## Goal

To automate the creation of emotionally engaging, story-driven Instagram post scripts (both caption and video formats) based on recent Formula 1 events and historical context. These scripts will be:

- Attention-grabbing within the first 2 seconds
- Designed for new F1 fans
- Emotionally resonant, curiosity-provoking, and algorithm-optimized
- Automatically paired with compelling media assets and published for maximum exposure

---

## Functional Components

### 1. **Analytics System ("The Analyst")**

#### Role

Act as a virtual F1 commentator capable of:

- Parsing recent race data via the FastF1 API
- Comparing with historical race patterns
- Detecting rivalries, drama, milestones, and statistical anomalies
- Synthesizing storylines based on trends and turning points

#### Sources

- [FastF1 API](https://github.com/theOehrly/Fast-F1)
- Internal caching system for historical data comparisons (last 2 seasons minimum)

#### Key Outputs

- Bullet-pointed insights tagged with emotional relevance
- Suggested narrative arcs: comeback stories, controversial moments, dramatic changes, underdog wins

---

### 2. **Composer Engine ("The Copywriter")**

#### Role

Transform insights into platform-optimized post/video scripts using LLMs (e.g., Sonnet3.7, GPT-4, Claude).

#### Output Formats

- Instagram Post Caption (text-only)
- Instagram Video Script (with caption timing/speaker lines)

#### Script Requirements

- Max Duration: 30 seconds
- Format: Punchy, 1-2 line sentences, emoji + hashtag optimized
- Hook: Must appear within first 2 lines/2 seconds
- Tone: Curious, dramatic, beginner-accessible
- CTA: Always includes a call-to-action (e.g., “Drop your hot take below 💥")
- Examples match @wtf1official or @f1dataanalysis styles

#### Output Example (Video Script)

```
[SPEAKER 1 - Caption: "Red Bull just got EXPOSED 😳"]
"Everyone thought Max had it in the bag."

[SPEAKER 2 - Caption: "But lap 43 changed EVERYTHING."]
"Until one bold move flipped the race."

[SPEAKER 1 - Caption: "The comeback story no one saw coming 🚀"]
"Is this the new title fight? Or just a fluke?"

[CTA Slide: "Drop your prediction for the next GP 💥 #F1 #Formula1 #F1Drama"]
```

---

### 3. **Post Generator ("The Visualizer")**

#### Role

Pair scripts with engaging, high-impact media:

- Use royalty-free content scraped from verified public domains
- Generate images and video segments using APIs from OpenAI, Stability AI, RunwayML, etc.
- Add overlays and transitions for reel-style output
- Format according to Instagram specs (Reels/Stories/Posts)

#### Output Requirements

- Resolution and aspect-ratio suitable for IG Reels and Posts
- Brand-safe, F1-themed templates
- Text overlays matching script lines
- Compressed MP4 for upload

#### Content Sources

- Unsplash, Pexels (scraped)
- AI-generated imagery using latest APIs
- Internal clip library from previous posts

---

### 4. Poster Module ("The Publisher")

#### Role

Automate secure posting to Instagram via Facebook Graph API

#### Features

- Uses Instagram Content Publishing API ([link](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/instagram-platform/instagram-api-with-facebook-login/content-publishing/?utm_source=chatgpt.com))
- Access tokens securely stored and rotated
- Auto-schedules posts for optimal timing
- Adds pre-defined hashtags, location tags, and @mentions
- Logs status of each post with fallback notification on failure

#### Exposure Optimization Techniques

- Smart posting windows (based on prior engagement)
- Caption-first vs. media-first testing
- Engagement bait CTA + pinned comment trick
- Alt-text for accessibility and ranking

